+    def rebuild_buffers(self, device=None, dtype=None):
+        """Recompute inv_freq and the cos/sin cache from self.dim and self.base.
+
+        All three are registered persistent=False, so they are absent from the
+        checkpoint. transformers 5.x builds the model on meta tensors and then
+        materialises anything the checkpoint did not supply -- and materialising
+        a meta buffer allocates memory without writing to it, so these come back
+        as whatever was on the heap. Observed on a fresh load:
+
+            inv_freq[:3] == [1.19e-26, 0.0, 0.0]
+
+        which makes cos non-finite and every attention output NaN, at layer 0,
+        on the very first forward. The model loads, reports the right shapes and
+        the right weights, and emits pure token soup.
+
+        5.x does re-initialise rotary buffers -- modeling_utils._init_weights has
+        a branch for it -- but only for modules carrying `original_inv_freq`,
+        `rope_type` and `config`, which is the shape of transformers' own rotary
+        class, not this one. So this class rebuilds itself and _init_weights
+        below calls it.
